 "transcript": [
  "[says] (to O-lan) Wang Lung responds to O-lan's question about the money.",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"It is the little red mouth of Lotus that I give it to. It is she that I will buy the gold pin for. It is she that I will buy the little red paper and the little red paper with a gold border and the gold paper.\"",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"And for my wife, why, she has the big red mouth of the earth and I will buy her---\"",
  "[silence] (to Wang Lung) O-lan says nothing.",
  "Wang Lung: \"I will buy red paper for my land and red paper for my ox and red paper for my grandfather's head, for he must have red paper on his head, and for my father's head and for my mother's head and for my aunt's head and for my uncle's head.\"",
  "[silence] O-lan says nothing.",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"Well and well, for I will make a red paper festival in the land of Wang Lung this New Year.\"",
  "[silence] O-lan says nothing.",
  "[says] Wang Lung continues his list of red paper purchases.",
  "[silence] O-lan says nothing.",
  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"And the big red paper of my eldest son, and of my second son, and of my third son, and of my little fool---\"",
